  "id": "halcyontradeoffice",
  "note": "HALCYON TRADE OFFICE: consignments and freight futures, on Halcyon Boulevard.\n\nThe tile's prose: a narrow glass front on the boulevard, three storeys of it, with the Halcyon eye\netched into the door and a strip of freight prices running green along the fascia.\n\nSo it is a narrow dark-clad block with a glazed front between two slim chrome piers. The ground\nfloor is the door and two lit panes either side, under a fascia that carries the prices as a green\nticker. Two bands of glass above are the upper floors, and the name is on the cornice, once. The\nflanks have narrow frosted slots, because the Trading Room has no windows.\n\nThe palettes are the Glasshouse's own (`ty_hf_chrome_dk` clad, `ty_volt_chrome` trim). None is in\nthe window-grid family.",
  "pal": "ty_hf_chrome_dk",
